\begin{frame}{Do pronouns mark ethnicity?}
  \begin{enumerate}
    \item Subject pronouns are consistently associated with Creole and Cajun identities
    \begin{itemize}
      \item Creole pronouns: mo, to, li, li, no, yé, to
      \item Cajun pronouns: je, tu, elle, il, on, ça (ils), tu
    \end{itemize}
    \item This effect is much clearer than between Indians and Cajuns
    \item Subject pronouns also appear to be associated with Black and White identities
  \end{enumerate}
\end{frame}